# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
pursuit	one
good	one
aims	one
# The move from P1 to C changes the order of the quantifiers. P1 says each pursuit aims at some good, possibly a different one for each. C says there is one good that every pursuit aims at.
# That is a fault in quantifier scope, not a change in what any word means. "good" and "aims at" mean the same in both statements, so I name no bridge.
